<title>INDIA: Protest strike keeps India soybean markets closed.</title>
<headline>Protest strike keeps India soybean markets closed.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean markets in central India remained closed on Wednesday due to an indefinite strike by traders protesting against an increase in local taxes.</p>
<p>A doubling of a market trading tax, mandi tax, from one to two percent and the imposition of another tax by local muncipalities and village councils has angered traders.</p>
</text>
